From: Oleg Keri <okerixx@gmail.com>
Date: Fri,  9 Oct 2026 10:26:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v2] soundwire: qcom: disable the interrupt before gating the
 clock
Message-Id: <20261009082639.22662-1-okerixx@gmail.com>

swrm_runtime_suspend() gates hclk straight after the ClockStopNow
broadcast, while the interrupt thread that completed it is still
clearing the status and CLK_STOP_FINISHED is about to fire. Both touch
registers with the clock going away; on x1e80100 and glymur hclk is the
SoundWire clock itself. The next clock-stop exit then fails at random
(bus clash, parity errors, AUTO_ENUM_FAILED) and one side of the
speakers stays detached until reboot.

Disable the interrupt before gating the clock and enable it again once
the clock is back.

Fixes: 74e79da9fd46 ("soundwire: qcom: add runtime pm support")
Signed-off-by: Oleg Keri <okerixx@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
[ A16 backport, snap2xee: the unmodified posting is
  soundwire-qcom-disable-irq-before-gating-clock-v2.mbox (patchwork
  14876178). FixItFoundry's rc5 queue reworked swrm_runtime_resume()
  (hclk enabled first, checked, and an err_clk path that gates it again),
  so the hunks don't apply as posted. Same two calls in the same places:
  enable_irq() right after hclk is enabled on resume, disable_irq() right
  before hclk is gated on suspend. Plus one disable_irq() in the new
  err_clk path before it gates hclk, which the posting's base doesn't
  have; without it a failed resume would leave the IRQ enabled with the
  clock off and the next resume would unbalance enable_irq(). ]
---
diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 689fb7a76..44450717c 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -2066,6 +2066,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	ret = clk_prepare_enable(ctrl->hclk);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
+	enable_irq(ctrl->irq);
 
 	if (ctrl->wake_irq > 0) {
 		if (!irqd_irq_disabled(irq_get_irq_data(ctrl->wake_irq))) {
@@ -2156,6 +2157,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 err_clk:
 	dev_err(dev, "runtime resume failed: %d\n", ret);
+	disable_irq(ctrl->irq);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
 	if (wake_irq_disabled)
 		enable_irq(ctrl->wake_irq);
@@ -2192,6 +2194,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		}
 	}
 
+	disable_irq(ctrl->irq);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(ctrl->hclk);
 
 	usleep_range(300, 305);
